From 261735b771a695502439bb1e02f47d44813a0de3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericman2001 <ericman2001@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:39:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/23] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: Use an identity domain for the
 X1E80100 ADSP

When Linux runs at EL2 without a hypervisor, as on Chrome OS devices
such as the HP Googlebook, nothing else sets up the ADSP's stream. Give
it an identity default domain, like the sc7180/sc7280 modems on Chrome
OS firmware. Where TrustZone provides a resource table, qcom_q6v5_pas
still attaches its own domain on top.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 795e8ec7e..00869dcc9 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -426,6 +426,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8250-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8450-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-adsp-pas" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-mdss" },
 	{ }
 };
